1
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:08,830
Howard Wolowitz.

2
00:00:08,830 --> 00:00:10,890
Hey, Howard. Dave Roeger here at NASA.

3
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:12,970
We need to talk about your upcoming mission.

4
00:00:12,970 --> 00:00:16,400
Yes, yes, I've been doing my push-ups.

5
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:20,170
I'm still stuck at nine, but...

6
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:25,490
...that's going all the way down with no one holding me.

7
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,010
That's great, uh, but that's not why I called.

8
00:00:29,010 --> 00:00:30,900
We've run into a bit of a snafu.

9
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:33,380
Your Soyuz capsule failed the pressurization test,

10
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:36,800
so bottom line, mission's been scrubbed.

11
00:00:38,770 --> 00:00:41,240
You're kidding. So what does that mean?

12
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:48,540
Boy, I got to tell you,

13
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:49,990
I'm really disappointed.

14
00:00:49,990 --> 00:00:54,000
This was my dream ever since I was a little kid.

15
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:57,910
Okay, well, uh,  thanks for the call.

16
00:00:58,610 --> 00:01:00,310
Yep, you, too.

17
00:01:01,390 --> 00:01:03,100
Yes! Thank you!

18
00:01:06,510 --> 00:01:09,040
I'm not gonna die in space!

19
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:13,130
I'm gonna die the way God intended,

20
00:01:13,130 --> 00:01:16,500
in my late 50s, with a heart full of pastrami.

21
00:01:43,530 --> 00:01:46,190
I'm going to need a larger shirt.

22
00:01:49,970 --> 00:01:52,330
This one's a little tight under the arms.

23
00:01:52,330 --> 00:01:53,420
Okay.

24
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:55,010
Do you think maybe it's tight

25
00:01:55,010 --> 00:01:56,830
because you're wearing long underwear?

26
00:01:56,830 --> 00:01:58,970
Yes, of course that's why it's tight.

27
00:02:00,450 --> 00:02:01,880
All right, let me rephrase the question.

28
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:03,480
Why are you wearing long underwear?

29
00:02:03,490 --> 00:02:04,920
You're kidding.

30
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:08,370
Shouldn't the question be: why aren't you?

31
00:02:09,110 --> 00:02:11,160
No, it should be: why are you?

32
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:14,900
Leonard, these rental tuxedos have been

33
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:17,710
worn by hundreds of sweaty strangers.

34
00:02:17,710 --> 00:02:19,930
I don't like my own sweat touching my skin,

35
00:02:19,930 --> 00:02:21,480
how do you think I feel about theirs?

36
00:02:22,710 --> 00:02:23,930
Why don't you slip this on?

37
00:02:23,930 --> 00:02:26,050
Said the hangman offering a noose.

38
00:02:27,670 --> 00:02:30,830
Well, that wasn't as entertaining as when he rents bowling shoes,

39
00:02:30,830 --> 00:02:32,620
but it was right up there.

40
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:34,940
Well, that's it.

41
00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:36,780
My orders have been rescinded.

42
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:39,260
I am officially "no go" to space.

43
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:41,420
I'm sorry, Howard, but I got to tell you,

44
00:02:41,420 --> 00:02:43,310
I'm a little relieved you're not going.

45
00:02:43,310 --> 00:02:44,450
Why?

46
00:02:44,450 --> 00:02:46,010
Come on, you were gonna go up in a rocket

47
00:02:46,010 --> 00:02:48,400
designed in the 1960s by the Russians.

48
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:49,770
Yeah, so?

49
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:51,520
When was the last time you were at Best Buy

50
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:53,780
and you heard someone say, "ooh, check out this Blu-ray player,

51
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:55,920
it must be good, it was built in Russia"?

52
00:02:58,270 --> 00:03:00,670
Well, their technology isn't that bad.

53
00:03:00,670 --> 00:03:03,250
When you come back to Earth in a Soyuz capsule,

54
00:03:03,250 --> 00:03:06,730
you free-fall from space at 500 miles per hour,

55
00:03:06,730 --> 00:03:08,360
and the only thing that slows you down

56
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,980
is a little parachute that pops out

57
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:11,620
right before you crash into the ground.

58
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:14,090
And the whole thing was designed by the same brilliant minds

59
00:03:14,090 --> 00:03:17,330
who were unable to capture Rocky and Bullwinkle.

60
00:03:19,610 --> 00:03:20,750
All right, well, whatever.

61
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:22,060
I wasn't worried.

62
00:03:22,060 --> 00:03:23,150
You weren't?

63
00:03:23,150 --> 00:03:27,070
Let me explain the difference between you and me.

64
00:03:27,070 --> 00:03:29,120
You watch Star Trek

65
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:30,420
I live it.

66
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:34,770
Oh, please. I don't remember the episode of Star Trek

67
00:03:34,770 --> 00:03:36,310
where the guy never goes to space

68
00:03:36,310 --> 00:03:38,720
and brags about it in a tuxedo store.

69
00:03:38,950 --> 00:03:40,350
Make all the jokes you want,

70
00:03:40,350 --> 00:03:42,520
but there's only one of us here brave enough

71
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:45,060
to almost do what I almost did.

72
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,210
Ah, much better.

73
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:52,390
You must be burning up.

74
00:03:52,390 --> 00:03:55,340
A little. But not more than your urethras will be

75
00:03:55,340 --> 00:03:57,750
after whatever's in those pants swims up them.

76
00:04:01,710 --> 00:04:05,210
I cut quite the dashing, yet hygienic figure, don't I?

77
00:04:05,210 --> 00:04:08,200
I look like the Flash about to get married.

78
00:04:11,870 --> 00:04:13,280
Oh! A tissue! A tissue!

79
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,650
Oh, good Lord!

80
00:04:15,950 --> 00:04:17,040
Uh, where's he going?

81
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:19,400
He keeps emergency Purell in the car.

82
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:20,940
Keys! Keys! Keys!

83
00:04:25,550 --> 00:04:26,890
- Hey, you. - Before I come in,

84
00:04:26,890 --> 00:04:29,260
you should know, I have gas.

85
00:04:30,970 --> 00:04:33,230
For the record, not your worst opening line.

86
00:04:33,230 --> 00:04:35,130
Check it out. It's the gas I use

87
00:04:35,140 --> 00:04:37,470
in my free-electron laser to support high voltages.

88
00:04:37,470 --> 00:04:40,980
But it also has an interesting secondary use.

89
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:44,120
Here. Breathe this in.

90
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,150
B-Before I do it,

91
00:04:45,150 --> 00:04:47,000
