140
00:06:54,810 --> 00:06:57,040
With our friends moving forward in their relationships,

141
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:59,790
I've decided that we should make progress in ours as well.

142
00:06:59,790 --> 00:07:01,610
Oh, dear Lord.

143
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:04,760
Two years ago, we didn't even know each other,

144
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:07,890
and now I'm in your apartment after dark.

145
00:07:09,050 --> 00:07:11,330
How much faster can this thing go?

146
00:07:12,450 --> 00:07:14,000
I had a feeling you'd be reluctant,

147
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,220
which is why I'm going to dip

148
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:17,270
into my neurobiological bag of tricks.

149
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:20,680
Oh, you brain monkeys kill me. Dip away.

150
00:07:22,030 --> 00:07:23,530
I have devised an experiment

151
00:07:23,530 --> 00:07:25,860
that I believe will increase your feelings for me

152
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:27,410
in an accelerated time frame.

153
00:07:27,730 --> 00:07:29,800
And how do you propose to do that?

154
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:30,680
Uh, hope you're not thinking

155
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:33,140
about some sort of LSD thought control.

156
00:07:33,970 --> 00:07:36,800
Because there's only one mind-expanding drug that this man enjoys,

157
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:38,380
and that's called school.

158
00:07:39,830 --> 00:07:42,590
Human beings form emotional attachments as they grow up.

159
00:07:42,590 --> 00:07:45,640
In your case, to your mother, superheroes, et cetera.

160
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:48,040
I'm going to attempt an experiment that

161
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:50,610
will get you to transfer those feelings to me.

162
00:07:50,620 --> 00:07:53,390
Well, seems what's on the menu tonight

163
00:07:53,390 --> 00:07:56,140
is malarkey with a big side of poppycock.

164
00:07:57,220 --> 00:07:58,050
We'll see.

165
00:07:58,050 --> 00:08:00,780
Let's start with a little romantic dinner music, shall we?

166
00:08:05,150 --> 00:08:07,240
Super Mario Bros.theme?

167
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:08,260
Yes.

168
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:11,150
I see what you're doing.

169
00:08:11,150 --> 00:08:13,360
You're attempting to build on the work of Ebbinghaus

170
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:16,700
by triggering an involuntary memory of me playing that game--

171
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:19,850
admittedly the happiest 600 hours of my childhood...

172
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:22,520
 ...but it won't work.

173
00:08:22,630 --> 00:08:25,290
Fine. There's no reason we still can't have a lovely dinner.

174
00:08:25,290 --> 00:08:26,660
Why don't you have a seat.

175
00:08:33,020 --> 00:08:34,710
May I offer you something to drink?

176
00:08:34,710 --> 00:08:36,280
You know I don't drink.

177
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:37,630
Not even...

178
00:08:37,630 --> 00:08:39,010
strawberry Quik?

179
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:42,750
I love strawberry Quik.

180
00:08:43,950 --> 00:08:45,950
It's my favorite pink fluid,

181
00:08:46,670 --> 00:08:48,810
narrowly beating out Pepto-Bismol.

182
00:08:50,110 --> 00:08:51,420
Oh, I know.

183
00:08:51,420 --> 00:08:53,110
I think it will go nicely

184
00:08:53,110 --> 00:08:54,790
with what I have prepared...

185
00:08:55,860 --> 00:08:57,100
for dinner.

186
00:08:57,100 --> 00:09:00,060
Spaghetti with little pieces of hot dog cut up in it!

187
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:02,350
Just like your mommy used to make.

188
00:09:03,130 --> 00:09:05,210
Oh... yummy, yummy!

189
00:09:05,210 --> 00:09:07,720
We should do this more often.

190
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:16,840
Uh-oh.

191
00:09:19,460 --> 00:09:20,400
I'm sorry. I did,

192
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:22,310
I crossed a line. I didn't mean to!

193
00:09:22,310 --> 00:09:24,810
Who says something like that right in the middle of sex?!

194
00:09:24,810 --> 00:09:26,120
I don't know, it just came out.

195
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:28,550
People say weird things during sex all the time.

196
00:09:28,550 --> 00:09:30,880
Okay, well, they sure as hell don't say that.

197
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:32,190
- It was the heat of the moment. - No,

198
00:09:32,190 --> 00:09:35,120
the heat of the moment is, "Ooh, yeah, just like that,"

199
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:37,070
not "will you marry me?"

200
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:40,400
I'm sorry.

201
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:41,970
Just-just give me another chance.

202
00:09:41,970 --> 00:09:43,540
Why, so you can crawl under the covers and go,

203
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:44,930
"Hey, baby, want to go look for houses

204
00:09:44,930 --> 00:09:46,960
in neighborhoods with good schools?"

205
00:09:49,060 --> 00:09:50,670
Again, I'm sorry.

206
00:09:50,670 --> 00:09:53,050
You know, with Howard and Bernadette getting married,

207
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:54,980
I got caught up in a little wedding fever.

208
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:56,060
I take it back.

209
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:58,380
You can't take something like that back.

210
00:09:58,380 --> 00:10:00,160
I mean, what are we even supposed to do now?

211
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:02,960
Okay, at some point, we'll look back

212
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:05,890
and this is going to be a funny story.

213
00:10:06,490 --> 00:10:08,240
Why don't we just start doing that now?

214
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:10,300
- You're kidding. - No.

215
00:10:10,940 --> 00:10:13,510
Hey, do you remember...

216
00:10:14,670 --> 00:10:19,070
 ...that time when I proposed to you in bed?

217
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:23,800
And you were all, like, "What are you doing?"

218
00:10:24,990 --> 00:10:26,820
That was so funny.

219
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:29,710
So funny.

220
00:10:31,180 --> 00:10:32,430
It's not funny.

221
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:34,730
Give it a minute.

222
00:10:36,830 --> 00:10:39,160
Is that a little smile I see there?

223
00:10:39,570 --> 00:10:41,070
I should go.

224
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:45,440
Hey, I was thinking.

225
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:47,630
For our first dance at the wedding,

226
00:10:47,630 --> 00:10:50,860
what if we learn the final number from Dirty Dancing?

227
00:10:52,300 --> 00:10:53,650
- You're kidding. - No,

228
00:10:53,650 --> 00:10:54,990
come on.

229
00:10:54,990 --> 00:10:56,450
How cool would that be?

230
00:10:56,450 --> 00:10:58,820
Me running into your arms...

231
00:11:00,570 --> 00:11:02,520
you lifting me up into the air.

232
00:11:04,630 --> 00:11:06,360
Oh, you're in a good mood.

233
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,760
Yeah, well, why wouldn't I be?

234
00:11:07,760 --> 00:11:10,230
You know, I'm marrying the girl of my dreams,

235
00:11:10,230 --> 00:11:11,960
and I finally got my mother to agree

236
00:11:11,970 --> 00:11:13,500
not to come on our honeymoon.

237
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,310
Oh, it's NASA.

238
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:21,690
Wolowitz.

239
00:11:22,230 --> 00:11:24,630
Oh! Hi, Dave. What's up?

240
00:11:26,690 --> 00:11:28,880
No kidding. Really?

241
00:11:30,010 --> 00:11:33,560
Well, that's...great news.

242
00:11:33,750 --> 00:11:35,580
Great, great news.

243
00:11:36,610 --> 00:11:41,000
All right, I'll watch my e-mail for the details.

244
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:43,600
Okay, talk soon.

245
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:46,720
What's so great?

246
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:50,400
It looks like I'm going into space after all.

247
00:11:50,700 --> 00:11:53,210
Oh, Howie, that's wonderful!

248
00:11:53,210 --> 00:11:55,210
Uh-huh, wonderful.

249
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:05,680
What happened? I thought they canceled your mission.

250
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:06,540
Th-They did.

251
00:12:06,540 --> 00:12:11,220
But NASA really wants my telescope up on the space station,

252
00:12:11,220 --> 00:12:14,280
so they're putting me on an earlier launch.

253
00:12:14,280 --> 00:12:18,140
- When?  - A...week from Friday.

254
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:21,200
What? We're getting married that Sunday.

255
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:23,540
You're right!

256
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:25,520
I-I can't go to space.

257
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:27,370
I have to get married,

258
00:12:27,370 --> 00:12:28,920
and no one can say that's not a good reason.

259
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:30,110
I'll call him back.

260
00:12:32,530 --> 00:12:35,310
Wait. I don't want to be the one who stands in your way.

261
00:12:35,310 --> 00:12:37,130
Well, too bad, you already did. It's a done deal.

262
00:12:37,130 --> 00:12:38,450
Oh, well. But I forgive you.

263
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:41,590
No. That's not how I want to start our marriage,

264
00:12:41,590 --> 00:12:43,040
