265
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:44,930
We'll have the wedding when you get back.

266
00:12:44,930 --> 00:12:49,250
But wh-what about all the plans and the guests?

267
00:12:49,250 --> 00:12:50,600
We'll call them.

268
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:52,490
Although my dad's gonna go a little nutso

269
00:12:52,490 --> 00:12:54,520
over losing his deposits.

270
00:12:55,270 --> 00:12:58,380
You're right, he is!

271
00:12:58,380 --> 00:13:00,750
Your dad's gonna be furious.

272
00:13:00,750 --> 00:13:03,330
There's no way he's gonna let us postpone this wedding.

273
00:13:03,340 --> 00:13:04,720
Well, we tried.

274
00:13:06,100 --> 00:13:07,240
I'll talk to him.

275
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:08,970
He won't say no to his little girl.

276
00:13:08,970 --> 00:13:12,760
No! I-I should talk to him,

277
00:13:12,760 --> 00:13:14,110
man to man.

278
00:13:14,110 --> 00:13:15,740
But, Howie, my dad can be a bully.

279
00:13:15,740 --> 00:13:18,030
He's gonna make you cancel your space flight.

280
00:13:18,030 --> 00:13:19,320
We can only hope...

281
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:20,900
that he doesn't.

282
00:13:23,370 --> 00:13:26,710
Bishop to queen four,

283
00:13:26,710 --> 00:13:28,520
level two.

284
00:13:29,250 --> 00:13:30,450
Check.

285
00:13:30,450 --> 00:13:31,730
Sheldon...

286
00:13:32,270 --> 00:13:33,900
knight takes bishop.

287
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:35,600
You all right?

288
00:13:35,930 --> 00:13:37,570
I'm fine.

289
00:13:38,690 --> 00:13:39,820
Are you?

290
00:13:39,820 --> 00:13:41,860
You left your queen exposed from above,

291
00:13:41,860 --> 00:13:43,650
you trapped your knight in the corner,

292
00:13:43,650 --> 00:13:46,680
and you keep sighing and saying, "Why me?"

293
00:13:48,930 --> 00:13:50,490
Very well.

294
00:13:50,490 --> 00:13:53,390
Can I ask you a question about women?

295
00:13:55,300 --> 00:13:56,610
We got you that book last year.

296
00:13:56,610 --> 00:13:58,230
Wasn't everything in there?

297
00:13:58,980 --> 00:14:02,900
No, I'm having a relationship problem with Amy.

298
00:14:02,900 --> 00:14:05,470
And by the way, that book gave me nightmares.

299
00:14:07,460 --> 00:14:08,850
Well, if it makes you feel any better,

300
00:14:08,850 --> 00:14:11,620
I screwed things up pretty good with Penny.

301
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:13,850
Look at us, Leonard...

302
00:14:13,850 --> 00:14:15,430
engaging in the social convention of

303
00:14:15,430 --> 00:14:18,050
men bellyaching about their ol' ladies.

304
00:14:19,430 --> 00:14:20,710
I guess we are.

305
00:14:20,710 --> 00:14:23,760
So, what's going on?

306
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:25,400
Believe it or not,

307
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:27,910
Amy has embarked on a campaign

308
00:14:27,910 --> 00:14:30,150
to increase my feelings for her

309
00:14:30,150 --> 00:14:32,210
by making me happy.

310
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:37,720
I'm sorry, that must be very difficult for you.

311
00:14:38,610 --> 00:14:39,740
It's awful.

312
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:41,800
This morning, she arranged for me

313
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:44,820
to be an Amtrak junior conductor for the day.

314
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:46,920
It-It's usually only open to children.

315
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:48,700
She got them to make an exception.

316
00:14:50,110 --> 00:14:51,570
Shame on her.

317
00:14:53,010 --> 00:14:54,990
They let me blow the whistle, Leonard.

318
00:14:56,250 --> 00:14:57,710
She's good.

319
00:14:58,150 --> 00:15:00,940
I know. And it gets worse.

320
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:02,840
Her efforts are causing me

321
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:04,990
to have affectionate feelings for her

322
00:15:04,990 --> 00:15:07,390
at inappropriate times.

323
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:13,280
You mean, like in bed or in the shower?

324
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:14,510
No!

325
00:15:14,510 --> 00:15:17,800
Would you please stop referencing that infernal book?

326
00:15:19,020 --> 00:15:20,920
For example, this morning,

327
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:23,160
I was calculating the random motion

328
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:25,160
of virtual particles in a vacuum,

329
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:28,070
when suddenly the particles morphed

330
00:15:28,070 --> 00:15:31,380
into an image of Amy's dandruff...

331
00:15:34,790 --> 00:15:37,510
...gently cascading down onto her pale,

332
00:15:37,510 --> 00:15:39,730
slightly hunched shoulders.

333
00:15:41,850 --> 00:15:44,030
What has that vixen done to me, Leonard?

334
00:15:44,870 --> 00:15:46,550
And how do I make it stop?

335
00:15:46,550 --> 00:15:48,820
Well, if you had a physical relationship,

336
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:50,850
I'd say propose during sex.

337
00:15:50,850 --> 00:15:52,770
Turns out that's a real mood killer.

338
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:56,520
- I assume we're talking about you now?  - Yeah.

339
00:15:56,550 --> 00:15:57,840
So, that's how this works?

340
00:15:57,840 --> 00:16:00,190
I complain, and then you complain,

341
00:16:00,190 --> 00:16:02,380
and no one offers any solutions?

342
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:05,400
Pretty much.

343
00:16:06,300 --> 00:16:08,330
Well, no wonder the women are winning.

344
00:16:12,750 --> 00:16:14,990
Mr. Rostenkowski, are you busy?

345
00:16:14,990 --> 00:16:17,810
Oh, just looking at some old pictures. Come on in.

346
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:19,340
Family pictures, or...?

347
00:16:19,340 --> 00:16:21,610
H-Holy crap, that's a dead person.

348
00:16:22,650 --> 00:16:24,720
Last murder case before I retired.

349
00:16:25,630 --> 00:16:27,790
How many bodies do you see there?

350
00:16:27,790 --> 00:16:28,910
Careful,

351
00:16:28,910 --> 00:16:30,890
it's a trick question.

352
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:33,380
I'm not sure.

353
00:16:33,380 --> 00:16:34,860
Nah, you'll never get it.

354
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:36,940
It's a fraction.

355
00:16:38,450 --> 00:16:39,870
How about that.

356
00:16:40,130 --> 00:16:41,160
Anyway, sir,

357
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:43,930
I need to talk to you about something.

358
00:16:44,250 --> 00:16:45,290
Walnut?

359
00:16:47,010 --> 00:16:48,020
No, thank you.

360
00:16:48,020 --> 00:16:49,160
 I'm allergic.

361
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:50,510
Oh, sure.

362
00:16:50,510 --> 00:16:52,910
My partner used to have that.

363
00:16:52,910 --> 00:16:54,610
He's dead now.

364
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:57,560
From nuts?

365
00:16:57,560 --> 00:16:59,350
Nah, his wife shot him.

366
00:17:00,530 --> 00:17:02,860
But she was nuts, so in a way...

367
00:17:05,330 --> 00:17:06,370
Nice story.

368
00:17:06,370 --> 00:17:07,420
Anyway,

369
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:10,750
the reason I wanted to talk to you is

370
00:17:10,750 --> 00:17:15,720
NASA has moved up my launch to the International Space Station.

371
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:17,310
- Yeah, so? - So...

372
00:17:17,310 --> 00:17:21,820
the date is going to conflict with me marrying your daughter.

373
00:17:21,820 --> 00:17:23,410
Now, I know what you're going to say--

374
00:17:23,410 --> 00:17:26,280
I made a commitment to Bernadette and to your family

375
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:28,540
and I've got a hell of a lot of nerve coming in here

376
00:17:28,540 --> 00:17:30,320
and demanding that we postpone this thing.

377
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:32,120
Well, message heard and understood.

378
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:33,710
Mission canceled. Thank you.

379
00:17:35,290 --> 00:17:36,470
Where are you going?

380
00:17:36,470 --> 00:17:38,090
I'm sorry.

381
00:17:38,090 --> 00:17:39,910
May I be excused?

382
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:42,070
No, you may not.

383
00:17:42,070 --> 00:17:43,530
Let me tell you something.

384
00:17:43,530 --> 00:17:45,240
When I first met you...

385
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:47,060
You just gonna stand there?

386
00:17:48,310 --> 00:17:50,850
I'm sorry, I didn't know, is this going to...

387
00:17:50,850 --> 00:17:51,860
Well, I should sit...

388
00:17:51,860 --> 00:17:53,650
May I be seat... Well, I'll just sit.

389
00:17:56,190 --> 00:17:58,060
When I first met you,

390
00:17:58,060 --> 00:17:59,540
I didn't like you.

391
00:18:00,660 --> 00:18:02,750
I'm aware of that, sir.

392
00:18:03,470 --> 00:18:06,140
But then you and I had some time together.

393
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:09,540
It did not get better.

394
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:12,350
Right, right.

395
00:18:12,350 --> 00:18:14,610
That silly Beatle haircut

396
00:18:14,610 --> 00:18:17,900
and...you riding around on a red Vespa,

397
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:20,570
and you're still living at home with your mother.

398
00:18:20,730 --> 00:18:23,550
To be honest, I thought Bernadette chose you

399
00:18:23,550 --> 00:18:25,140
to punish me.

400
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:29,580
But then I heard about your astronaut thing,

401
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:31,170
and I realized

402
00:18:31,640 --> 00:18:33,800
I judged you too fast.

403
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:36,840
Maybe you are the right guy for my little girl.

404
00:18:36,840 --> 00:18:39,200
Oh, I am. And just so you know,

405
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:42,470
I'd still be an astronaut, even if I didn't go to space.

406
00:18:42,550 --> 00:18:44,800
 I've got an I.D. card and a NASA golf shirt.

407
00:18:46,100 --> 00:18:47,730
No, no, you got to go.

408
00:18:47,730 --> 00:18:50,160
You can't turn down an opportunity like this.

409
00:18:50,160 --> 00:18:52,440
B-But what about the wedding

410
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:55,080
and all the money you put down for the reception?

411
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:56,800
You let me worry about that.

412
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:58,770
You go up to that space station,

413
00:18:58,770 --> 00:19:00,870
and you make me proud.

414
00:19:05,470 --> 00:19:07,090
Um, okay.

415
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:09,980
You got a problem with that?

416
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:12,240
All right, look, I'm gonna level with you.

417
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:15,820
I'm terrified about going into space.

418
00:19:15,820 --> 00:19:19,010
What if I don't make it back?

419
00:19:19,590 --> 00:19:22,120
It's gonna be okay, son.

420
00:19:23,800 --> 00:19:25,420
You really think so?

421
00:19:25,420 --> 00:19:26,910
Of course.

422
00:19:26,910 --> 00:19:29,650
A pretty girl like Bernadette...

423
00:19:29,650 --> 00:19:32,200
she'll find a new guy.

424
00:19:43,070 --> 00:19:44,180
- Off to work?  - Yeah.

425
00:19:45,260 --> 00:19:46,650
Have a nice night.

426
00:19:46,650 --> 00:19:48,210
Okay, you, too.

427
00:19:48,640 --> 00:19:50,640
Penny, just, wait.

428
00:19:51,520 --> 00:19:52,560
I've been thinking about what I said

429
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:54,380
when we were in bed the other night.

430
00:19:54,380 --> 00:19:56,570
Yeah, I've been thinking about it, too.

431
00:19:56,570 --> 00:19:58,790
I noticed you never answered me.

432
00:20:00,230 --> 00:20:01,610
You're right.

433
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:08,840
No.

434
00:20:11,340 --> 00:20:13,890
- Uh, follow-up. Are we still dating?  - Yep.

435
00:20:14,450 --> 00:20:17,040
- Is it still weird 'cause I proposed? - Yep.

436
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:19,720
 I have a couple more quick questions.

437
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:21,850
- Do you want to call me from the car? - No!

438
00:20:24,980 --> 00:20:26,930
Think I played that pretty well.

439
00:20:39,510 --> 00:20:41,060
Hello, Leonard.

440
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:43,090
What are you doing?

441
00:20:43,090 --> 00:20:44,640
We're playing doctor.

442
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:48,660
Star Trek style.

443
00:20:50,310 --> 00:20:52,420
I'm in hell, Leonard.

444
00:20:54,610 --> 00:20:56,620
Don't stop.

